Usage Guide
Configuration
All settings live in `src/fomcConfig.m`.
Field	Default	Purpose
`useSampleData`	`true`	`false` downloads real minutes from federalreserve.gov
`startYear`, `endYear`	2023, 2025	Year range for downloads
`useNeuralEmbeddings`	`true`	`false` forces the TF-IDF fallback
`embeddingModel`	`all-MiniLM-L12-v2`	Or `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`
`usePostgres`	`false`	`true` stores vectors in PostgreSQL with pgvector
`topK`	5	Passages retrieved per question
`llm.Provider`	`auto`	`auto`, `openai`, `ollama`, or `extractive`
`customQuestion`	`""`	Extra question answered after the validation set
`showFigures`	`true`	`false` for headless runs
Run with real minutes
```matlab
cfg = fomcConfig();
cfg.useSampleData = false;
cfg.customQuestion = "Why did the Committee change the policy rate?";
runFOMCPipeline(cfg);
```
Downloaded pages are cached in `data/downloads/`. If nothing can be downloaded, the pipeline falls back to the sample data.
The questions in `data/sample/questions.csv` are written for the sample data. For real minutes, supply your own
`questions.csv` (columns `Question`, `ExpectedMeeting`, `ExpectedKeywords` separated by `;`) and set `cfg.questionsFile`.
`ExpectedMeeting` for downloaded minutes looks like `fomc_20250129`.
PostgreSQL with pgvector
```bash
docker run --name fomc-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres -p 5432:5432 -d pgvector/pgvector:pg16
```
```matlab
setenv("FOMC_PG_PASSWORD", "postgres");
cfg = fomcConfig();
cfg.usePostgres = true;
runFOMCPipeline(cfg);
```
`sql/schema.sql` shows the schema the pipeline creates (vector dimension 384 for all-MiniLM).
LLM answers
```matlab
setenv("OPENAI_API_KEY", "sk-...");
```
or run a local model with Ollama and set `cfg.llm.Provider = "ollama"`. Install "Large Language Models (LLMs) with MATLAB"
from the Add-On Explorer, or clone https://github.com/matlab-deep-learning/llms-with-matlab and add it to the path.
Without an LLM, answers are the top retrieved passages.
Validation metrics
HitRateAtK: fraction of questions whose expected meeting appears in the top-k passages.
MRR: mean reciprocal rank of the first passage from the expected meeting.
MeanKeywordRecall: share of expected keywords found in the retrieved passages.
MeanAnswerCoverage: share of expected keywords found in the generated answer.
Tests
```matlab
runtests("tests")
```
